# Cloudflare redirects, one per line: <old path> <new path> <status>
# "/*" matches the old multi-page versions (/2/, /3/ ...) of an article too.
#
# Only old URLs with a genuinely related page on the new site are redirected.
# Everything else from the old site gets the custom 404 page, which is what
# Google expects for content that no longer exists.

# Old WordPress articles (2023-2025)
/11-bad-financial-habits-that-are-keeping-you-poor     /psychology  301
/11-bad-financial-habits-that-are-keeping-you-poor/*   /psychology  301

# Old magazine site (2020-2022)
/business/online-trading-meet-the-traders-who-became-millionaires-from-working-at-home/*  /options  301
/business/robinhood-trading-app-gamestop-hedge-funds-wall-street-retail-investor-deal/*   /psychology  301
